1
00:00:01,260 --> 00:00:05,920
Now your friends have no idea my Stand
Crush has quite a handy little helper.

2
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:10,000
Yes, my Stand Talking Mouth works wonders,

3
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:12,817
especially when it latches
onto your tongue and

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:16,076
forces you to say the exact
opposite of what you mean.

5
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:22,717
Narancia, that must be the reason why
you can't give us a straight answer.

6
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:23,682
It's the enemy.

7
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:34,990
Giorno!

8
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:40,660
Whatever that stand is,

9
00:00:40,860 --> 00:00:42,497
it's dragging Giorno into that puddle of

10
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:45,227
water like a ravenous
shark ready for dinner!

11
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,720
Lil' Bomber!

12
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:53,757
That bloodthirsty beast
can jump from liquid

13
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:56,197
to liquid and somehow
take Giorno with him,

14
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:58,633
no matter the amount of liquid there is!

15
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:01,937
Mmm, that bite was juicy.

16
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:03,160
Now to end it.

17
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:07,007
If we can take Giovanna and his
life-giving stand out of play,

18
00:01:07,260 --> 00:01:12,025
killing the rest of these perdenti will
be as easy as falling off a swirling log.

19
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:13,090
So true.

20
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:14,697
Everything's going swimmingly.

21
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:17,000
However, we shouldn't dawdle.

22
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:20,317
Let's choke the life form from
the boy and be done with it.

23
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:25,060
Our intel says Narancia's stand is
a bonafide carbon dioxide detector.

24
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:28,184
So you may have well
knocked Giorno unconscious,

25
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:33,017
but given that he's still breathing, your
stand is still on Lil' Bomber's radar.

26
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:36,040
Even your puddle jumping
won't escape his notice.

27
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:41,501
The last thing we want is that puny plane
finding us and giving them the upper hand.

28
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:43,660
They'd be on us in seconds.

29
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:46,700
Yes, I agree, Tiziano.

30
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:49,340
Giorno will breathe no more.

31
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,260
I'll make sure of it

32
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:34,180
Thank you.

33
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,480
Yeah, I got you!

34
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,540
Oh, shit!

35
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:28,821
That thing is gonna take
Giorno away and kill him!

36
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:32,300
Damn this bastardo.

37
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:37,780
Instead of one stand to deal with, there
have been a pair of stands all along.

38
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:39,250
God!

39
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:40,330
Ah!

40
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,200
Oh, damn it!

41
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:47,077
I can't hit this guy for shit!

42
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:51,336
And the more I miss my mark, the more
chances I'm giving him to escape!

43
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:57,140
I've got to start anticipating his
moves! Where is he? Where'd he go?

44
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,110
There!

45
00:04:02,193 --> 00:04:04,397
He can teleport till
he's blue in the face!

46
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:07,480
As long as I stay one step
ahead of him, I can win!

47
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:10,340
The boy's using his radar again.

48
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:13,160
As I said, he seeks to find and kill us.

49
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:15,657
We have to halt Giorno's
breathing immediately.

50
00:04:15,740 --> 00:04:16,980
Simmer down.

51
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,769
It's under control, Teets.

52
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:24,500
But you know, attacking Giorno while
teleporting isn't exactly a walk in the park!

53
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:28,200
Now we're in sync! Fire!

54
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:32,740
I hit his neck!

55
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:37,950
Giorno!

56
00:04:38,033 --> 00:04:39,200
I'm so sorry!

57
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:40,680
I didn't mean to...

58
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,097
What the hell?!

59
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:46,080
His breathing!

60
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:48,341
I'm not picking up his breathing!

61
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:52,774
Why isn't the radar detecting anything?

62
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:55,020
Son of a bitch!

63
00:04:55,280 --> 00:04:56,820
He got away from me!

64
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,100
Well, he's a goner now.

65
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,797
Crush has taken him for
a ride in the sewer.

66
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:06,762
I'll have it swim to the canal and
dump off the dead weight there.

67
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,900
Hang on a sec, Squalo.

68
00:05:09,140 --> 00:05:10,097
What the hell was that?

69
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:11,010
Huh?

70
00:05:11,093 --> 00:05:13,017
I was just saying that I'd dump his body.

71
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:13,930
Not that.

72
00:05:14,013 --> 00:05:14,860
I mean Narancia.

73
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:17,512
It was far away, but I know what I heard.

74
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:19,977
It was Narancia's voice
shouting something.

75
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:22,884
He was screaming about
it getting away from him.

76
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:24,090
Huh?

77
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:27,377
Right now, Talking Mouse should
still be affixed to his tongue.

78
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:30,357
There's no way the kid should
still be able to speak the truth.

79
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:32,337
How in the hell did he choke that out?

80
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:35,057
He even said the radar
wasn't picking anything up.

81
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:36,100
Move, Squalo!

82
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:38,097
You have to get away from there now!

83
00:05:38,180 --> 00:05:39,257
What are you talking about?

84
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:42,217
I guarantee you Giorno's
never gonna breathe again.

85
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:44,437
There's no way anyone
can snip out Crush now.

86
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:46,097
I think it might be overreacting.

87
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:48,239
No, he said it got away on purpose.

88
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:51,117
He did it in order to
make you drop your guard.

89
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:55,435
Can't you see he was trying to get
you to stall your next teleportation?

90
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:58,297
For the life of me, I
don't know how he did it,

91
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:01,498
but the bastards found a
way to track your movements.

92
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:04,310
That's it.

93
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:07,267
Giorno moved into my
line of fire on purpose.

94
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:10,797
He used the gun smoke to
give me a trail one that'll

95
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:13,960
lead me right back to the
enemy It's crystal clear.

96
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:16,720
I can see that stinking guppy a mile away.

97
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:17,870
All right

98
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:31,757
How do you like that hate to ruin your
plans But you're no still hasn't been the

99
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:36,257
big one if we can revive him in the next
few minutes We might be able to save him!

100
00:06:36,340 --> 00:06:37,811
We're in trouble, Squalo!

101
00:06:37,940 --> 00:06:40,257
He's already nailed you
twice with that gun,

102
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:43,340
so all he has to do is
follow the smoke back to us!

103
00:06:48,660 --> 00:06:49,490
Yes!

104
00:06:49,573 --> 00:06:51,536
I drove the scumbag out of the sewer!

105
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:54,320
Well, I'm stuck, Bucciarati.

106
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:57,477
This is about as far back
as I can go with this guy.

107
00:06:57,560 --> 00:07:02,031
Based on the replay, our attacker was
in the cup on this table at one point.

108
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:04,920
But whatever it was, it left in a hurry.

109
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:06,790
Unfortunately,

110
00:07:06,873 --> 00:07:10,477
Moody Jazz can't transform beyond
this time, and it can't move either.

111
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:12,537
What are you trying to say, Abakyo?

112
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:13,660
I'm not sure.

113
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:16,437
It's almost like this thing can teleport.

114
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:18,440
This bastard's got me stumped.

115
00:07:18,620 --> 00:07:21,137
I just can't replay
enough to see the user.

116
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:24,102
It's like the videotape
has been severed somehow.

117
00:07:26,180 --> 00:07:27,010
Damn it!

118
00:07:27,093 --> 00:07:29,217
I didn't think Narancia was this clever!

119
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:31,140
He's not, it was Giorno!

120
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:35,617
We're in this mess because he decided to
let himself get mauled by Lil' Bomber.

121
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:38,137
We played into his hands
and didn't even know it.

122
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:39,050
Come on!

123
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:41,144
I can't get rid of the residue!

124
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:43,777
It must be because he was
hit with stand bullets.

125
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:46,389
Even the water can't
get this grunt off me!

126
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:49,377
I've got to find somewhere to hide.

127
00:07:49,460 --> 00:07:52,342
Somewhere his detectors
won't be able to find me.

128
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:04,076
Great, we're playing this game again.

129
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:05,700
All right, think!

130
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:10,117
This ugly-looking shark thing may have
crazy speed for a long-range stand,

131
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:14,297
but from what I've seen, it can't get
very far with one of its teleports.

132
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:17,086
It can only move two to
three meters per jump!

133
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:20,370
Shit!

134
00:08:21,580 --> 00:08:22,540
Oh, man!

135
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:26,568
He's predicting my moves and
his aim is getting more precise!

136
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:29,117
He's slowing down!

137
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:31,260
It must be his injuries!

138
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,200
Squalo, no!

139
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:40,500
Yeah, I got him!

140
00:08:40,780 --> 00:08:43,898
Just one more direct hit
and then it's bye-bye fishy.

141
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:46,180
Now go to hell, you bottom feeder!

142
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:51,280
What's that smell?

143
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:53,320
There's a gas leak!

144
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:56,897
This is all going according
to plan, Narancia.

145
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:59,020
Thanks to your ace shooting,

146
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:02,692
the hot water spilt out of the
pot and put out the flames.

147
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:06,157
How's a little bomber gonna shoot
me in this gaseous death trap?

148
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:09,477
My quick thinking has rendered
your tracking skills a moot point.

149
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:12,325
But by all means, fire
away and ignite the gas.

150
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:14,217
Doing so might not kill you,

151
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:16,337
but everything around you
will be set ablaze and

152
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:19,538
the resulting carbon dioxide
will nullify your radar.

153
00:09:21,660 --> 00:09:23,013
What's wrong, Narancia?

154
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:25,260
You seem to be hesitating.

155
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:28,370
Shoot already!

156
00:09:28,453 --> 00:09:29,680
Secure our victory!

157
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:33,100
So what if I can't shoot your ass to hell?

158
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:39,640
There are plenty of ways
to fillet a homicidal fish!

159
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:42,660
I did it!

160
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:43,958
I finished him off!

161
00:09:44,180 --> 00:09:46,356
Bucciarati, Mista, the enemy is here!

162
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:50,915
Abacchio, he has the ability to
transport himself from liquid to liquid!

163
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:54,240
Good, he's breathing again.

164
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:58,080
Hang on, I just told the truth.

165
00:09:58,480 --> 00:10:00,715
I've regained control over what I say.

166
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:03,000
It's been done.

167
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:07,437
I've gone ahead and released Talking
Mouth from Narancia just as you planned.

168
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:09,285
This was a brilliant strategy.

169
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:15,074
You've sustained several injuries,
but I'm sure the boss will be pleased.

170
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,497
What's all the racket, Narancia?

171
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:21,237
You said you found the enemy?

172
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:24,026
But Talking Mouth's
release is only temporary.

173
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:25,937
Why is Joino...

174
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:27,549
Is that the enemy's stand?

175
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:31,537
Oh, no!

176
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:32,700
Wait, don't!

177
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:35,640
This is how you secure
victory, my dear Squalo.

178
00:10:36,160 --> 00:10:38,240
It's time to complete our mission.

179
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:39,677
Here we go, six bullets!

180
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:41,100
Fire away, mister!

181
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:48,400
What the hell just happened?

182
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:00,470
Shit!

183
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:02,180
My radar's going crazy!

184
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:04,893
He's gonna strike and I can't track him!

185
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:09,569
That bastard's gonna kill Giorno all
because I can't tell the freaking truth!

186
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:13,560
Narancia, you have to look for it.

187
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:15,820
Giorno, you're awake!

188
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:17,550
The user.

189
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:22,440
Forget the stand and go
after the stand's user.

190
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:24,460
Giorno, look out!

191
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:35,200
Hey, Narancia!

192
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:36,700
You idiots,

193
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:38,477
why in the hell would
you give me the all-clear

194
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:41,384
to shoot when this place
is a ticking time bomb?

195
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:46,480
Watch out! There it is!

196
00:11:46,660 --> 00:11:47,954
The enemy's above you!

197
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:49,930
No!

198
00:11:50,013 --> 00:11:51,520
He's below you, damn it!

199
00:11:54,140 --> 00:11:54,970
What the?

200
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:58,880
This is so messed up.

201
00:11:59,220 --> 00:12:00,300
I'm screwed.

202
00:12:00,580 --> 00:12:02,097
The lies just keep coming.

203
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:03,651
I've got to stop talking.

204
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:05,420
He's gone.

205
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:07,641
No doubt he'll kill Giorno first.

206
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:10,409
Then he'll start wiping
out the rest of us.

207
00:12:10,820 --> 00:12:11,650
The user.

208
00:12:12,020 --> 00:12:13,800
Forget the stand and go after.

209
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:16,020
The stand's user.

210
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:17,790
Giorno.

211
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:24,159
Giorno told me to go after the user

212
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:25,350
That's right,

213
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:28,557
the user's injured Which
means he's probably

214
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:31,540
breathing pretty heavily
at the moment Of course,

215
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:35,053
that's it He wants me to use
my radar to find the bastard

216
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:40,880
I've gotta do this And it's gotta
be on my own Now, where is he?

217
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:45,967
I know the guy's a long-range stand user
But he has to be around here somewhere

218
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:47,600
I'm out of time!

219
00:12:47,860 --> 00:12:49,300
This fool dies now!

220
00:12:58,460 --> 00:13:00,940
The plan's going off without a hitch.

221
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:05,833
With Giorno out of the picture, they
won't be able to play doctor anymore.

222
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:08,520
Now drive the nail in Giorno's coffin.

223
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:10,120
His time's come.

224
00:13:10,780 --> 00:13:12,060
It'd be my pleasure.

225
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:13,717
I'm not quite at my best.

226
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:17,565
But I still have enough juice
left to knock him to kingdom come.

227
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,780
Hey, look. It's Narancia.

228
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:24,771
What's he doing out here?

229
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:27,520
Where exactly is Crush right now?

230
00:13:28,420 --> 00:13:29,480
It's over there.

231
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:34,764
It went out of the sewer, over by the
restaurant, and is heading toward the canal.

232
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:37,372
He shouldn't be able to track it anymore.

233
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:41,457
Surely he couldn't be trying
to hunt me down, could he?

234
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:43,397
My breathing should be untraceable.

235
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:44,310
It's madness!

236
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:45,920
Calm yourself, Squalo.

237
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:47,520
No need to fear.

238
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:51,540
All this is just his feeble
attempt at victory. Tell me,

239
00:13:51,780 --> 00:13:56,427
how many pedestrians do you think are
walking around this hundred meter radius?

240
00:13:56,700 --> 00:13:58,420
Fifty? A hundred?

241
00:13:58,900 --> 00:14:02,488
He can't tell you from anyone
else walking around down there.

242
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:06,100
But I'm injured.

243
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:09,157
What if he picks up on the
unnatural breathing and

244
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:12,299
decides to follow that trail
all the way back to me?

245
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:15,000
You have to collect yourself.

246
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:17,077
Look at the bottom of the stairs.

247
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,517
Several people down there are
breathing a lot harder than you,

248
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:23,894
so all you need to do is allow
your breathing to settle.

249
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:28,517
If we walk into that piazza like nothing
is wrong, everything will work out.

250
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:31,188
Fact of the matter is,
we've won this fight.

251
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:32,860
Yeah, you're right.

252
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:35,005
We've got this in the bag now.

253
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:37,440
There's no way Flyboy can find us.

254
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:40,000
I've got you, Stronto!

